hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"142","Yahya bin Habib Al-Harithi and Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Dhabi narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas Al-Laythi, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Actions are based on intention, and a person only has what he intended. So whoever’s emigration is to God and to His Messenger, his emigration is to God and to His Messenger, and whoever’s emigration was for a worldly gain or a woman to marry, his emigration is for what he emigrated to.” Ahmad did not say: A man only does what he intended."
"143","Narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Walid, by Abdul-Wahhab, meaning Ibn Abdul-Majid Al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: Muhammad bin Ibrahim, that he heard Alqamah bin Waqqas Al-Laythi, saying: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Actions are based on intention, but a person only does what he intends.”"
